OLMo-1B-0724-hf:
I have the following C++ class : 
 class CcdImageList : public std::list  > 
The Swig object is correctly transmitted to the Python, but I cannot iterate on the list. 
What should I do (in Swig ? )  to make it iterable ?

A: In order to use C++ class in Python, make sure you have a C++ class with non-virtual destructor. If you don't have a good reason to use non-virtual destructor, the following code will work:
class CcdImageList : public std::list >
{
public:
    CcdImageList() : std::list() {}
    CcdImageList(const CcdImageList &other) : std::list(other) {}
    CcdImageList & operator=(const CcdImageList &other) { std::list::operator=(other); return *this; }
    ~CcdImageList() { }
};

The destructor is not virtual as it's non-virtual.

