OLMo-2-0425-1B-Instruct:
I have the following C++ class : 
 class CcdImageList : public std::list  > 
The Swig object is correctly transmitted to the Python, but I cannot iterate on the list. 
What should I do (in Swig ? )  to make it iterable ? 

Here is the code where I try to iterate on it :

```cpp
#include "CcdImageList.h"

for (auto &value : CcdImageList::get()) {
    // stuff...
}
```

This code does not work because the `CcdImageList` is not implemented to be iterable.

**Solution:** Use `swig_py_list` instead of `std::list<>`. `swig_py_list` is a Swig type that is designed to be iterated over.

Here is the modified code:

```cpp
#include "CcdImageList.h"

swig_py_list<CcdImageList> imageList;
for (auto &value : imageList) {
    // stuff...
}
```

